### ==========================================
### 1. Exercise Creation (Existing Test)
### ==========================================
POST http://localhost:3000/exercise/create_exercise_choice HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "exercise": {
        "description": "กรุณาเลือกคำตอบที่ถูกต้อง",
        "level": 1,
        "expectTime": 60,
        "skillId": 1
    },
    "exerciseChoices": [
        {
            "choiceNo": 1,
            "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 1",
            "isAnswer": true
        },
        {
            "choiceNo": 2,
            "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 2",
            "isAnswer": false
        },
        {
            "choiceNo": 3,
            "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 3",
            "isAnswer": false
        },
        {
            "choiceNo": 4,
            "script": "ตัวเลือกที่ 4",
            "isAnswer": false
        }
    ]
}

### ==========================================
### 2. KT-IDEM Flow via NestJS Gateway (:3000)
### Flow: Client -> NestJS (:3000) -> FastAPI (:8000)
### ==========================================

### 2.1 Register Skill via NestJS
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/skill HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "skillId": "control_flow",
  "pL0": 0.3,
  "pT": 0.2
}

### 2.2 Register Item via NestJS
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/item HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "itemId": "cf-for-01",
  "skillId": "control_flow",
  "pG": 0.25,
  "pS": 0.1,
  "difficultyLabel": 2
}

### 2.3 Submit Attempt via NestJS (Student answers correctly)
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/attempt HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "std_001",
  "itemId": "cf-for-01",
  "correct": true
}

### 2.4 Submit 2nd Attempt via NestJS (Student answers incorrectly)
POST http://localhost:3000/kt/attempt HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentId": "std_001",
  "itemId": "cf-for-01",
  "correct": false
}

### 2.5 Get Student Mastery via NestJS
GET http://localhost:3000/kt/mastery/std_001/control_flow HTTP/1.1


### ==========================================
### 3. Direct FastAPI Endpoints (:8000)
### For directly testing python microservice
### ==========================================

### 3.1 Health Check
GET http://localhost:8000/health HTTP/1.1

### 3.2 Register Skill Directly (snake_case)
POST http://localhost:8000/kt/skill HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "skill_id": "math_algebra",
  "p_l0": 0.2,
  "p_t": 0.15
}

### 3.3 Register Item Directly (snake_case)
POST http://localhost:8000/kt/item HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "item_id": "alg-01",
  "skill_id": "math_algebra",
  "p_g": 0.2,
  "p_s": 0.15,
  "difficulty_label": 1
}

### 3.4 Submit Attempt Directly (snake_case)
POST http://localhost:8000/kt/attempt HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "student_id": "std_002",
  "item_id": "alg-01",
  "correct": true
}

### 3.5 Get Student Mastery Directly
GET http://localhost:8000/kt/mastery/std_002/math_algebra HTTP/1.1



